# model_block.tas — place a half block (a block with a baked model).
#
# Purpose: show the model mesher in the demo. Hotbar slot 5 holds the
# half block (`slab` in examples/voxel/content.zig). Its baked model is a
# box from y 0 to y 0.5, so the model mesher meshes it, and the greedy
# mesher meshes the full cubes around it (REQ-VOXEL-001).
#
# Scene (flatland, the same spawn each run): the player looks down 30 degrees,
# selects slot 5 and places the half block on the ground in front. A
# second right-click on the same spot places a full stone block on top of
# the half block: the top quad of the half block has no cull face, so it
# stays, and the stone shows its bottom face over the gap.
#
# Usage (from the repo root):
#   zig build native -Dexample=voxel
#   ./zig-out/bin/voxel --world=flatland --aa=none \
#     --tas examples/voxel/tests/model_block.tas \
#     --dump-frame=model_block.ppm
#
# Expected: a pale blue-grey half block on the grass in front of the
# crosshair, half the height of a full block. With `--headless` and no
# dump, the run exits 0.
#
# Tick numbering is relative to the first post-loading tick.

# --- Capture mouse ---
1 mouse_down left
2 mouse_up left

# --- Look down about 30 degrees (the same as hotbar_place.tas). ---
3 mouse_move 0 180

# --- Select slot 5 (the half block). ---
8 keydown 5
9 keyup 5

# --- Place the half block on the targeted ground block. ---
14 mouse_down right
15 mouse_up right

# --- Hold steady so --dump-frame lands on a stable view. ---
30 mouse_move 0 0
